<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Prague (1635)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1635</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of Prague was concluded on 30 May 1635 between Emperor Ferdinand II and Elector John George I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, and most Protestant princes of the Empire soon joined it. Saxony gained Upper and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-lusatia">Lower Lusatia</a>, the Edict of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/repatriation-of-cultural-property">Restitution</a> was effectively suspended, and the princes' armies were to unite under the emperor. It failed to end the war, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> continued.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peace-of-prague-1635.jpg" alt="Peace of Prague (1635)" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frans Luycx · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Georg_I_Saxony.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
